# API Design Standards

## Resource Naming

RESTful, plural nouns, nested for relationships:

```
GET    /books                    # list all books
POST   /books                    # upload a new book (multipart)
GET    /books/{id}               # get book details + processing status
DELETE /books/{id}               # remove a book
POST   /books/{id}/chat          # send a chat message (SSE stream response)
GET    /books/{id}/chapters      # get book structure / TOC
POST   /books/{id}/quizzes       # generate a quiz
GET    /books/{id}/progress      # get study progress
```

## Response Models

Every endpoint returns a Pydantic model -- never a raw dict or untyped JSON.

```python
class BookResponse(BaseModel):
    id: str
    title: str
    status: ProcessingStatus
    chapters: list[ChapterSummary]
    created_at: datetime

@router.get("/{book_id}", response_model=BookResponse)
async def get_book(book_id: str, db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)) -> BookResponse: ...
```

## Streaming (SSE)

Chat endpoints return `text/event-stream` via `StreamingResponse`:

```python
from sse_starlette.sse import EventSourceResponse

@router.post("/{book_id}/chat")
async def chat(book_id: str, req: ChatRequest) -> EventSourceResponse:
    return EventSourceResponse(stream_agent_response(book_id, req))
```

## Pagination

List endpoints accept `?page=1&limit=20` and return:

```python
class PaginatedResponse(BaseModel, Generic[T]):
    items: list[T]
    total: int
    page: int
    limit: int
```

## File Uploads

- Use `UploadFile` with content-type validation (`application/pdf`)
- Enforce max file size in middleware (default 100MB)
- Return processing status immediately; process async in background

## Documentation

Every route function has a docstring used as the OpenAPI description. Include `response_model`, `status_code`, and `summary` parameters.
